  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "University email verification is required for registration",
    "File storage uses AWS S3 for scalability and file_url stores the S3 path",
    "Study groups have optional maximum member limits (max_members can be null for unlimited)",
    "Ratings are on a 1-5 star integer scale",
    "Notifications support real-time delivery via WebSockets",
    "Users can belong to multiple study groups (many-to-many via group_members junction table)",
    "Each note can have multiple ratings from different users (one rating per user per note)",
    "Soft delete may be implemented for notes and groups using a deleted_at column if needed",
    "The average_rating in notes table is calculated from the ratings table and updated when new ratings are added",
    "A unique constraint on (note_id, user_id) in ratings table should prevent duplicate ratings from the same user",
    "A unique constraint on (group_id, user_id) in group_members table should prevent duplicate memberships",
    "The role column in users table uses varchar to support extensibility for future roles",
    "Indexes are created on foreign keys and frequently queried columns for performance optimization"
  ]
}